<title>HUNGARY: Hungary auctions 5 bln forint of 7-yr bonds Jan 2.</title>
<headline>Hungary auctions 5 bln forint of 7-yr bonds Jan 2.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 5 billion forint worth of seven-year government bonds of the 2003/F series on January 2, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Friday.</p>
<p>    Date of issue		17 October 1996</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   24 September 2003</p>
<p>    Bills on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	  103.14 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction (Dec 19)	103.64 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a floating interest rate, calculated on March 20 and September 20 every year adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. Interest is paid once a year, on September 24. The starting interest is 25.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
